---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import Steps from '../../components/Steps.astro'
import { VaultReplica } from '../../components/app/Replicas'
---
<Base title="Saving a credential - Sanctum guide" description="Add a login, reveal it when you need it, and copy the password without leaving it in Windows clipboard history.">
  <section class="section wrap" style="border-top: none;">
    <h2>Saving a credential</h2>
    <p>The Vault holds logins. Each one has a name, a username, a password, a URL, notes and tags.</p>
    <Steps steps={[
      'Open <strong>Vault</strong> and click the <strong>+</strong> button.',
      'Fill in the name and username. Only the name is required &mdash; an entry you cannot identify is worse than an untidy one.',
      'Type the password, or click <strong>Generate</strong> for one that meets the strength floor.',
      'Save. The password is encrypted before it touches disk and is never returned by the list.',
    ]} />
    <VaultReplica />
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>Getting it back out</h2>
    <p>
      The eye icon reveals one password at a time. The copy icon puts it on the clipboard through a
      guarded path: Windows clipboard history and cloud sync are both told to exclude it, and it is
      cleared automatically after thirty seconds.
    </p>
    <p>
      If Windows reports it kept its own copy anyway, Sanctum tells you rather than staying quiet.
      Press <kbd>Win</kbd> + <kbd>V</kbd> if you want to check for yourself.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section wrap">
    <h2>Folders and favourites</h2>
    <p>
      Folders group entries by client or project. They are scoped per module, so a folder in the
      Vault is separate from one in Notes or Env Files &mdash; one client with all three needs a
      folder in each. Favourites cut across everything and are the fastest way back to what you
      touch daily.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
